      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5b52ba672b29a515be8ff219|full_name}: a voice changer worth using costs money, and VRC is currently free. For VRC to use an existing voice changer would cost licensing fees, for VRC to make a voice changer from scratch would be prohibitively expensive. Both of these options would cost money that VRC is not currently bringing in and do not affect the core purpose of VRC. Since VRC is  a  tool for socialization and a media for self expression with worlds and avatars, if making your voice sound different is part of your self expression, then it is your responsibility to acquire the needed SW for that to happen. VRC supplies you the frame work for visual representation of you expression, additionally they provide audio interface for you to play music or speak. All of this is already provided for free. Voice changing technology is hard to do, there are a very small number of decent sounding changers out there, and lots of changers that do 1 or 2 effects marginally well and that is it. It is not because people don't want them, its because it is exceedingly difficult to make it work in any meaningful way. Even the goods one take time to tweak the effects to get a decent sound out of them. I cannot tell you how many times I've had to tell someone I've met that I cannot understand them and they need to adjust their settings or turn it off to continue the conversation. Voice changing SW is out there, if you feel you need it, buy it of pirate it, asking that it be included with a free SW is asking for something that will either sound like complete garbage or VRC would have start charging for access.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
