      "mergeID": "637e9fa53ee45d7d0c3467d3",
      "mergedPostDetails": "So, this is something that's already on Rec Room, but with all of the people on VRChat experimenting with identity and even the front page proudly talking about this, I think it would be great for trans people to have an in-game voice changer so they don't get misgendered as often. In a game that brags about being able to be whoever you wish to be, being able to change the way your voice sounds in-game would take that one step further for people who can't afford things like hormone therapy, or even people who just want to feel more immersed in their character, especially since modded clients that may have included a voice changer are now banned.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Add voice changing",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5a458089a20b4579cfd61778",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "What a fantastic idea!",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
