  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2017-12-28T23:38:49.610Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "first part is pretty self-explanatory. Basic effects for pitch, reverb, etc. Simple stuff to get by.\n\nReason I suggest it being part of vrchat instead of a separate app (besides convenience) is the idea of giving avatars default settings to fit in with their characters. Robots sounding tinny, small avatars sounding high pitch, big/ghostly avatars having an echo and so on. Something avatar creators could set in Unity and that user can disable if they don't like the change. ",
